          "equivalence": "bit-identical",
          "optimizationLog": "Loop interchange i/j/k -> i/k/j with __restrict pointers. Streams B[t][0..n] sequentially across each row instead of striding 512 B down columns, while accumulating each cell in ascending t = 0..k-1 order (-ffp-contract=off). Bit-identical to the strict-f32 oracle. Measured 1.21x over the C Track A baseline (0.8971 ms -> 0.7419 ms, 128^3, arm64 macOS).",
          "maxUlpDeviation": null,
          "maxRelativeDeviation": null,
          "declaredTolerance": null
        },
        {
          "key": "c-tiled",
          "baseline": "c",
          "equivalence": "bit-identical",
          "optimizationLog": "32x32 i/j panel cache blocking with the inner k reduction left intact so each cell accumulates in ascending t = 0..k-1 order. Bit-identical to the strict-f32 oracle. Measured 0.97x (0.8971 ms -> 0.9250 ms) at 128^3 because the 64 KiB B matrix already fits in 128 KiB L1d while the inner loop still strides B down columns.",
          "maxUlpDeviation": null,
          "maxRelativeDeviation": null,
          "declaredTolerance": null
        },
        {
          "key": "c-ikj-simd",
          "baseline": "c",
          "equivalence": "bit-identical",
          "optimizationLog": "Loop interchange i/k/j combined with -msimd128 (-ffp-contract=off). On the baseline i/j/k loop, -msimd128 yields 0.96x because LLVM cannot vectorize the inner t reduction without reassociating floating-point additions. Interchanging to i/k/j makes the inner j loop independent across columns, unlocking 4-wide f32x4 vectorization while every lane still accumulates in strict ascending t = 0..k-1 order (0 ULP deviation, bit-identical). Measured 4.43x over the C Track A baseline (0.8971 ms -> 0.2025 ms).",
          "maxUlpDeviation": null,
          "maxRelativeDeviation": null,
          "declaredTolerance": null
        },
        {
          "key": "c-simd-dot",
          "baseline": "c",
          "equivalence": "reassociated",
          "optimizationLog": "Explicit wasm_v128 (f32x4) 4-lane accumulation along the inner k reduction in i/j/k order, horizontally reduced via (lane0 + lane1) + (lane2 + lane3). Because each output cell sums 4 partial chains instead of a single left-to-right scalar chain, floating-point rounding differs from the strict-order oracle (max 31488 ULP / 0.002152 relative deviation on full-mantissa LCG inputs, within declared 0.005 tolerance). Measured 1.79x over the C Track A baseline (0.8971 ms -> 0.5021 ms) — slower than c-ikj-simd (4.43x) because gathering strided B elements into a vector register costs 4 scalar loads per step.",
          "maxUlpDeviation": 31488,
